Current original Zero workflow (0.12)

Use the native tools on Linux or their .exe versions on Windows:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
All destination paths must be new. The integrator preserves authored sources;
the builder checks its compiler fixed point and builds the original targets;
the verifier checks language behavior and host file operations in process.
See tools/integrate.ztext, tools/build.ztext and checks/README.ztext.
Read these documents with zero-text read FILE.

The notes below preserve earlier implementation and test history. Any old
shell/Python runner names, generated artifacts, JSON reports or commands are
historical references: they were removed from the active project and are not
current runnable instructions or current-release validation. Native host
checks do not replace BIOS/UEFI, persistence or physical-hardware testing.

Historical implementation notes

CANONICAL ZERO0.11 HOST DURABILITY EXTENSION

Current canonical compiler.zero adds filesync and hostwait to the16 existing
host operations. Newsource SHA256:
a76aeeda865a3fbbc887c3d9a66c8a02bd1ff5e46aacd1d359a361033c170b7a
Candidate ELF93086 bytes, three identical own-compiler generations, SHA256:
d89762ea95d3591d95e7f9a66e1015d8124bf87f702dac65ce25547f2ec4ed3f
Candidate artifacts and exact evidence: portability/host/durability.
Seed/build promotion and full OS integration are controlled by the release
coordinator. These component results do not by themselves establish a release.

136 focused checks pass: nativeLinux/Wine21-assertion probes, targetgating,
arity/reservednames, injectedEINTR retry andEIO/EFAULT failure paths, actual
x64 guest fallback execution, IA32 guest compilation, native Windows exact
compiler self-reproduction.433 common regressions and17Linux behavior cases
also pass, as do existing Windows61API/20boundary assertions and Unicode,
argv, cooperativeworker and Ezero host-file regressions. OwnWindows formatter
reproduces all updated Windows template values. app64 compiler94438 bytes;
app32 compiler124286 bytes; both fit existing131072-byte slots.

filesync requests file flushing only, not directory/rename crash durability.
hostwait suspends the current native thread for0..86400000 milliseconds.
Both return0/-1 on hosts and-1 on guests after evaluating operands. SeeABI.txt.

HISTORICAL ZERO0.10 HOST API INTEGRATION

The16-operation extension is published in canonical compiler.zero and the
normal own bootstrap/build binaries. The frozen0.9 release and its original
source/seed remain separately preserved; they were not rewritten.

Source86992 bytes, SHA256:
cf01adff93330c930d1fa6628bbc459d6e93a404b3196afa6ae783922ecc77b7
Executable91573 bytes, SHA256:
911f6d67361300755c13bbf5f3d231d54ceae5736f1ec5e60dde5d6e4095ed3a
Normal builds reproduce the fixed point. The transition from the preserved
0.9 seed reached identical generations2/3 after the original Linux entry
changed from41 to44 bytes; no external compiler or binary patcher was used.

Implementation parts and ABI are in this directory. apply-common.py records
the historical development integration and must not be reapplied to the
already merged source. Normal builds compile canonical compiler.zero directly.
Guest compiler images fit unchanged131072-byte slots:92925 x64,122307 IA32.
Current decoder32768 bytes and total reservation4022880 fit the4MiB arena.

Verification:
-433 common parser/gating/fallback checks, native x64 guest fallback execution;
-exact preserved raw/UEFI/real probe output and ordinary guest output parity;
-17 actual Linux API runtime cases, with byte-exact final-merge linkage;
-Windows native PE self-reproduction,61 API assertions,20 boundary assertions,
 Unicode/quoting/argument and cooperative-context tests under Wine10;
-native Zero compiler CLI and original setup-program tests, recorded separately.

Reports: verification/host-api; linux-verification.json;
windows-verification.json; windows-cli-verification.json; installer/verification.
No native Microsoft Windows machine or real Windows reparse fixture is claimed.
The reparse test is explicitly unverified because Wine's creation API is a stub.
Live source, syntax, limits and ownership are in LANGUAGE.ztext, SYNTAX.ztext,
